  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Truckin** (1 review): Opener moves from Truckin' into Smokestack Lighting and then returns to Truckin' [5]\n- **Help On The Way** (1 review): Reviewer ranks the Help > Slipknot > Franklin's sequence among the best they have heard [5]\n- **Morning Dew** (1 review): Reviewer calls this Morning Dew another tremendous version, worth the recording alone [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Smokestack Lighting**: rare: 14 archived performances [6]\n- **High Time**: rare: 13 archived performances [6]\n- **Watchtower**: rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- **Playin Reprise**: back after 67 archived shows (654 days) [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2023-06-10** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 199 min; rated 4.75/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer found the tempo of the performance very slow and draggy, comparing it to trudging through a desert; Recording is nearly flawless: clear, crisp, with well-balanced bass [2][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The Other One's second verse picked up from the prior night's first verse, and the Playin' reprise also completed the night before [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2023-06-10**: taped by Jeff Travitz [1]. Also: Taped by Jeff Travitz, who also recorded the previous Wrigley Field show [3]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Worthpoint: [Dead and & Company UNCUT Poster 2023 Wrigley Field Chicago Masthay 677/1000 | #4644040722](https://www.worthpoint.com/worthopedia/dead-company-uncut-poster-2023-4644040722) [7]",
